    "serial": {
        "baud_rate": 0,
        "comments": "{{:media:dlink:dir-885l:dir-885l_serial.jpg?400|Serial Port}}\n\nGeneral information regarding Serial ports and cables is provided [[docs:techref:hardware:port.serial|here]]. Located on the top side of the D-Link DIR-885L PCB is an unpopulated 4-pin header labelled JP1. This header is accessible without removing the top heatsink. When probed with a multi-meter, the results do not match the provided general information. However, this header still appears to be a serial port, with the following arrangement: Pin 1 (square) - Rx, Pin 2 - Vcc (3v3), Pin 3 - Gnd, and Pin 4 - Tx. In order to use it reliably, pins should be soldered to the header. **Caution:** This port operates at TTL voltage levels (3v3). Applying voltages greater than 3v3 will permanently damage the router.\n\n^  Serial Port Settings             ||\n| Speed                  | 115200    |\n| Data Bits              | 8         |\n| Stop Bits              | 1         |\n| Parity                 | None      |\n| Flow Control           | None      |\n|                        |           |\n|                        |           |\n\n**Note:** The console of the D-Link DIR-885L OEM firmware prior to v1.15b02 is **not** password protected. However, credentials are required to login into the console of later encrypted versions of this firmware. FIXME Please add them, if known.",
